+The Understanding Graph is a selective record, not a second model or truth
+oracle; it makes selected belief revisions addressable. Live
+access can support queries about stored state and return \texttt{Not Found},
+but cannot verify the world or claims the model never queries. Its readable
+record also offers a partial inspection point before successor training.
+Source checks, independent validation, mechanistic investigation, and
+governance remain necessary for that interface to be useful.
 
